@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Remote Manifest Store
  "Authoritative RMW for .mason/manifest.json under the site root with temp-file atomic commit."

  Provides:
    - remote.ManifestStore @source("symbol:ManifestStore")
    - remote.RemoteManifestStore @source("symbol:RemoteManifestStore")
    - remote.NewRemoteManifestStore @source("symbol:NewRemoteManifestStore")
    - remote.ManifestPath @source("symbol:ManifestPath")
    - remote.RemoteManifestStore.Fetch @source("symbol:Fetch")
    - remote.RemoteManifestStore.Put @source("symbol:Put")
    - remote.RemoteManifestStore.Update @source("symbol:Update")

  Consumes:
    - remote.RemoteFS
    - domain.ParseManifest
    - domain.MarshalManifest

  Invariants:
    - Fetch MUST return an empty v1 manifest when manifest.json does not exist yet
    - Put MUST write to manifest.json.tmp then atomically rename over manifest.json
    - Update MUST load, mutate, validate via MarshalManifest, and commit atomically

  Scenario (happy-path): First manifest
    Given no remote manifest file
    When Fetch runs
    Then an empty v1 manifest is returned without error

  Scenario (happy-path): Atomic update
    Given an existing manifest
    When Update mutates shares and commits
    Then the remote file is replaced via temp + mv

  Scenario (negative): Corrupt remote JSON
    Given invalid manifest bytes on the server
    When Fetch runs
    Then it returns a parse error
